{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go","id":54991,"title":"[Recruitment](Exaltled 2.5 Gunstar Autochthonia) To Boldly Go...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-21T15:59:55-08:00","id":54991,"title":"[Recruitment](Exaltled 2.5 Gunstar Autochthonia) To Boldly Go...","content":"Since there's a huge demand, it seems, for Exalted here, I'll be starting a new game. So, I'm not trying to step on Noodle's toes with this one. His game and the players are all cool people. This is mainly to A) Accommodate the demand I've seen, and B) I've always wanted to play in the Gunstar Shard, so here's that. <br /> <br /> So, here are my game thoughts:<br /> <br /> Plot: The PCs are all going to be members of a scouting team with an elder Alchemical starship to scout the Spiral and determine new resources the Line can use to build their arsenal further and plot positions of the Primordials within the Spiral itself. Positions within the team will be filled as the PCs determine their castes and favored areas, and so on.<br /> <br /> Allowed PC Types: Any Autochthonia-native Exalts will be allowed without question (Solar, Lunar, Sidereal, Alchemical, and DB) I'll be hesitant to allow GSPs, but since I'm an ST of a stripe that can't very well say &quot;No,&quot; if you present your case WHY your GSP has defected, then, I'll probably allow it, but ask beforehand, please, okay?<br /> Abyssals are off-limits, though.<br /> <br /> Circle size: Maximum of 6. <br /> <br /> Thanks, and I hope to get this rolling soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:03:59-08:00","id":54996,"title":"","content":"I am so in. I will likely end up playing a Sidereal Martial Artist. I know, I'm really breaking out of my comfort zone there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:06:57-08:00","id":55004,"title":"","content":"If I weren't still banging away at trying to get a character for Forging a Nation, I would be all over this. I have a Starmetal crafter out for vengeance against his traitorous Joybringer mentor/lover I've wanted to play for ages now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:09:11-08:00","id":55006,"title":"","content":"@Noodle: Whoa, man, don't go all crazy like that. You? A Sidereal Martial Artist? No way.<br /> <br /> @Jim: By all means, man. That sounds like a cool character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:18:03-08:00","id":55016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=55004#post55004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I weren't still banging away at trying to get a character for Forging a Nation, I would be all over this. I have a Starmetal crafter out for vengeance against his traitorous Joybringer mentor/lover I've wanted to play for ages now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry about it, Jim. I'm not going to get angry at you if you build a character for another game first. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=55006#post55006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Noodle: Whoa, man, don't go all crazy like that. You? A Sidereal Martial Artist? No way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right? A truly shocking development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:29:13-08:00","id":55024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=55006#post55006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By all means, man. That sounds like a cool character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I don't know, I'm not ready to give up on my inspiration for the other game just yet, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=55016#post55016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=55004#post55004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I weren't still banging away at trying to get a character for Forging a Nation, I would be all over this. I have a Starmetal crafter out for vengeance against his traitorous Joybringer mentor/lover I've wanted to play for ages now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry about it, Jim. I'm not going to get angry at you if you build a character for another game first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really do want to play with Omicron, though. He knows why I have my man-crush on him.<br /> <br /> (Also, in all fairness, &quot;banging away&quot; should be understood to mean &quot;staring morosely at a character sheet with a pencil in hand, doing nothing.&quot; Some days the creativity won't stop, and some days the gods point and laugh at you.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:38:25-08:00","id":55100,"title":"","content":"I understand, Jim. Sometimes, it takes time, but I don't think that the two games are mutually exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:21:34-08:00","id":55163,"title":"","content":"Question: what's the rough size of the scouting mission? Are you envisioning a small, dedicated team with a trim but proficient support team, or a full fleet and a significant portion of the Defense Line's resources put into this?<br /> <br /> Also, how far away is the Gunstar? Is this scouting mission a timid &quot;let's finally go see what the Spiral really is&quot; or a &quot;herald the Second Primordial War&quot;?<br /> <br /> All in all, consider me very interested! Right now I'm thinking of a Solar ace pilot angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:09:21-08:00","id":55202,"title":"","content":"Glad to have you, Jotun! To answer your questions, I was envisioning the scouting team as a single large vessel; a mobile Patropolis-level Alchemical used to accommodate a crew of a thousand or so DB enlisted personnel, and the officer cadre of the PCs/ NPCs that fill any missed niches should it be called for. <br /> <br /> To get to the second point, you'll be behind enemy lines, largely to scout out and see what the Spiral has been up to in the intervening years. So, more Column A than Column B as you put it. Don't worry, though. I won't leave you entirely without aid, even if it won't be the entirety of the Line fleet. <br /> <br /> Finally, don't worry about the space for voidtech fighters or the like. I am allowing all the neat toys that Gunstar allows, as we have more or less an entire city to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:13:09-08:00","id":55208,"title":"","content":"Okay, I have a pretty awesome character concept coming but first, I'd like to check something: can I get an Integrated God-Machine Grid (from the Viodfighter gunships) as a feature for a Celestial Battle Armor? Specifically, I want my dude Tekkaman Blade style power armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T03:06:51-08:00","id":55354,"title":"","content":"I am definitely interested in playing anything Exalted at this point. My two questions are this: First, what is the estimated game day/time that you have for this. Second, what is the medium you wish to game in? Forum, Skype, IRC, or G+ Hangout? As for character concept, I am thinking Sidereal Sword Master (akin to Gurney Hallek) Investigator (Batman!) type character. No real background yet as I haven't dealt much with the Gunstar shard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/385-savare","name":"Savare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T05:16:33-08:00","id":55384,"title":"","content":"Actually, I had a thought on the way into work. Given your title and theme is obviously a nod to Star Trek then maybe I should play Mr. Wolf - Tactical Officer (Full Moon Lunar) who loves his prune juice. haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/385-savare","name":"Savare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T07:14:59-08:00","id":55421,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, an Exalted Game, how nice... I'll need to come up with a character design that'll work though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2067-alectai","name":"Alectai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T07:53:44-08:00","id":55444,"title":"","content":"@Savare: Halleck, Batman (Albeit more as a Lore/Magitech Junkie than PREPTIME Batman), and Mr. Wolf are all excellent character ideas. To answer your question about the game's format, It'll be on the forum as a PbP. If you want to message me, I'm usually on in the mornings, PST.<br /> <br /> @Alectai: Glad to have you! If you want to shoot ideas for your character concept, feel free to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T08:30:34-08:00","id":55459,"title":"","content":"Well, that's just it, I had concepts for Modern, concepts for Heaven's Reach, and concepts for vanilla, but I didn't have any handy for Gunstar unfortunately :|<br /> <br /> Figuring out something I'd want to play as is going to be hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2067-alectai","name":"Alectai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T08:53:50-08:00","id":55479,"title":"","content":"@Noodle: Sorry for not addressing your question earlier. Yes, you can, but it'll count as one of your three subsystems. <br /> <br /> @Alectai: What is your concept you were going to use in Vanilla? Since it's the closest of the Shards you've mentioned to Gunstar, and can probably be retooled pretty easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T13:44:28-08:00","id":55661,"title":"","content":"Count me interested. I'll have to whip up a more concrete character concept. Probably a social Solar though.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Reading over things again, my thought go to an Eclipse Caste Diplomat. Being a &quot;Who knows what we'll find?&quot; kind of feel to exploring the spiral, he could be Picard as opposed to Kirk. So lots of social stuff, able to make a good first impression and read others well. I like the idea of him having his own personal voidfighter in case things get ugly. Total war calling for even the politicians to contribute to the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","user":"AlbztheDude","date":". 01-22-2014, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","name":"AlbztheDude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T15:21:43-08:00","id":55739,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately I am not really that into a play by post game so I guess you can count me out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/385-savare","name":"Savare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T15:32:58-08:00","id":55746,"title":"","content":"@AlbztheDude: Nice to have you on. A Picard would be a great addition.<br /> <br /> @Savare: That's too bad, but, I understand.<br /> <br /> Now, a thought for you all: Is there any locales or themes you'd want to explore in this? As Albz and a Savare have noted, my initial thoughts are planet-spanning romp akin to Star Trek TOS, but I'm open to doing other things, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T15:48:44-08:00","id":55758,"title":"","content":"First thing that comes to mind for me would be some spy work. Going to planets to gather potential allies while avoiding detection by the Infernals. Finding out whether others rebel against the Titans' rule, or even more interesting; finding that the systems of the Spiral have dedicated themselves to Total War against the Exalted just as we have against them.<br /> <br /> Also, any houerules we should know about for character gen? or just 2.5 errata?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","name":"AlbztheDude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T16:10:53-08:00","id":55781,"title":"","content":"I've been considering all those ideas, Albz, but spy-work would be fun to use, too.<br /> <br /> I don't have any houserules in mind, either, Do you have anything in mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T16:24:33-08:00","id":55787,"title":"","content":"A good mix between &quot;explore the legendary Spiral and see if it matches up to the hype&quot; and &quot;behind enemy lines&quot; is what I would put forward as a general idea. Spywork sounds great, but I'd also note that having a city-sized ship as home base is going to make it a challenge. I'm thinking that submarine-war fiction is actually not a bad source to look at. A shadow hunt between massive ships trying to find and destroy a single submarine that's more or less specifically hidden. As much 20,000 Leagues Under the Sea (which has the exploratory angle to boot) as Hunt for Red October.<br /> <br /> I would also suggest that there be a bit more of a specific mission goal. Just a few ideas: find a place in the Spiral where a more permanent (and likely hidden) base can be set up; friendly signal sent out from the Spiral with a need to find out where it's come from; Rescue Mission: Gnosis; etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","user":"Jotun","date":".  Getting my 40k and 20,000 Leagues mixed up. 01-22-2014, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T16:29:31-08:00","id":55790,"title":"","content":"I can agree with all the above.<br /> <br /> @Dietaku I didn't have anything in mind. Should we assume standard chargen then? Or will we be more experienced Exalts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","name":"AlbztheDude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T16:43:11-08:00","id":55797,"title":"","content":"Adding my voice in accent to Jotun's suggestions. Those are some pretty cool ideas.<br /> <br /> Character-wise, I'm leaning towards a Chosen of Secrets who has come to the conclusion that the Exaltations are the most powerful weapons in this war, so to win, we need to get as many of them as possible on our side. His plan is to weaponize the protocols built into the Loom that make every Exaltation that's within Fate to go to Autochthon. Specifically, he's going to hunt down GSPs and Celestial Akuma, Fate 'em and then cap 'em. <br /> <br /> If anyone wants to coordinate Backstories, I'm open to discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T16:56:36-08:00","id":55809,"title":"","content":"@Jotun: I hadn't considered Sub warfare, but that's a great idea. Another thought, is despite how huge your ship will be, the Spiral is vast, and the Titans you'll be fighting, bigger still, so I think it'll work.<br /> <br /> As for a more specific mission goal, you raise a good point, so here's what I have.<br /> <br /> Gunstar Era 5063, 1/23:<br /> From: Fleet Admiral Invictus Gladians Hime, Forward Gunline Fleet Commander<br /> To: Officer Corps of the Battle Patropoli, <i>Radical</i><i> Mendicant Zekka</i><br /> <br /> Alright, you dogs. The Top Brass has a mission for you of utmost importance. As you are no doubt aware, attacks by the Enemy have become more frequent, and so it has become imperative to strike back and hit them where it hurts the most. We're taking back the Spiral and moving back into strike at their means of production. To do so, we need a secure base of operations, and that's where you come in. Long-range Probe deities have indicated that the Western Arm has little in the way of overt military capabilities, considering its relative distance from Us. Thus, the plan will be as such. My main line will draw their attention away from the West, by making a feint towards the South. You and the Fast Cruiser, <i>Mercury's Delight</i>, will then break off and continue towards the West. You need to find a piece of real estate to let us move into.<br /> <br /> Once you've discovered an ideal planet, message the Fleet, and we'll move in. Til then, be on your guard, and by the Incarnae, don't start going in grand-standing. Your's is a mission of stealth and subterfuge, not fleet action, got it?<br /> <br /> I cannot stress to you the critical nature of this mission. Should this fail, and the Enemy discover our motives, you can rest assured that everything we've been fighting for will be for naught.<br /> <br /> Is that more what you were looking for, Jotun?<br /> <br /> @Albz: I figure that you're all going to be semi-experienced members of the Fleet, so you all get 50 Exp. Does that seem fair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","user":"Dietaku","date":". 01-22-2014, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T17:03:02-08:00","id":55815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlbztheDude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=55790#post55790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can agree with all the above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit, are you--are you the guy I played with in Troubled Waters back in the day?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T17:40:05-08:00","id":55845,"title":"","content":"Thanks Dietaku, that really helps!<br /> <br /> Still trying to flesh out a concept myself, but the more that this game develops, the more I'm leaning away from &quot;ace pilot&quot; and more towards an explorer/troubleshooter. Thinking Allan Quatermain and Odysseus influences, but still need to nail this down.<br /> <br /> Liking very much where this game idea is heading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T17:58:30-08:00","id":55856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jotun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=55845#post55845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Dietaku, that really helps!<br /> <br /> Still trying to flesh out a concept myself, but the more that this game develops, the more I'm leaning away from &quot;ace pilot&quot; and more towards an explorer/troubleshooter. Thinking Allan Quatermain and Odysseus influences, but still need to nail this down.<br /> <br /> Liking very much where this game idea is heading.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm now imagining Kirk with a gigantic rifle. Thanks for the hilarious mental image, and glad you like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T21:14:30-08:00","id":55928,"title":"","content":"@ JimB Ocean Fist yea. Good times. How'd that game end up going? I think we were both in Deathmatch's Alchemical game too. Where you tried to solo that Apostate and died.<br /> <br /> @ Dietaku I didn't have a particular number in mind or anything, but if 50 is what you think, I'll probably have him ready toromorrow. I just gotta fill in some backstory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","name":"AlbztheDude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T21:33:40-08:00","id":55938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlbztheDude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=55928#post55928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How'd that game end up going?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you know, pretty well. Saved the world and such. Ayende stole the Imperial Manse from the Scarlet Bride, which I feel pretty smug about. The game mostly ended because we all had elder Essence and the mechanics couldn't handle us any more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlbztheDude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=55928#post55928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we were both in Deathmatch's Alchemical game too. Where you tried to solo that Apostate and died.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer to think of it as a heroic sacrifice, rather than as me dying because I forgot what the hell my plan had been between game sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T07:58:46-08:00","id":56132,"title":"","content":"Sounds like you two have quite the common gaming history. That's cool, and I'm glad to have that camaraderie here. I just made the OoC thread for us. When your character is up, post them there. If you need to shoot ideas about your characters or their creation, however, discuss that in this thread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T08:19:04-08:00","id":56143,"title":"","content":"@Dietaku yea, we were in a couple of skype games that lasted for about a year before my schedule (ie. Getting a new job) forced me to bow out. Should I send a backstory/sheet to you first Dietaku? Or just post on the ooc thread for review?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","name":"AlbztheDude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T08:25:31-08:00","id":56150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlbztheDude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=56143#post56143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Dietaku yea, we were in a couple of skype games that lasted for about a year before my schedule (ie. Getting a new job) forced me to bow out. Should I send a backstory/sheet to you first Dietaku? Or just post on the ooc thread for review?</div> </div> </div> </div>Post it in the OoC thread, that way I can keep them all in one place for perusal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T11:44:20-08:00","id":56255,"title":"","content":"ST-man: If I take the Prodigy merit, will the Houserule where you get a 2-exp deduction on charms of that Ability in effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T11:48:24-08:00","id":56262,"title":"","content":"I'll allow it. MA is EXP-heavy enough as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T15:12:21-08:00","id":56375,"title":"","content":"Query regarding firearms. Are we using the default rules on pg 40 for Gunstar, ie no firearms, or are we opening that can of worms up and allowing it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T15:27:24-08:00","id":56383,"title":"","content":"I'm hesitant to allow &quot;True&quot; firearms. Call me a fluff purist, but the addition of guns to a world where bows can fire any distance with perfect accuracy, and be fired for any duration, seems a bit moot. However, the more I think about it, the more that I could also see the Spiral using them anyways. <br /> <br /> Alright. I'll allow firearms. However! They'll be used as a class of Archery weapons, so no Firearms charms, if that's understandable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T15:36:58-08:00","id":56389,"title":"","content":"I'm perfectly comfortable not having firearms and sticking to alchemical technology, but I wanted to know if we'd be dodging lazers and/or bullets in this setting. Either way, no firearm charms seems like a good compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T15:43:29-08:00","id":56391,"title":"","content":"The Starmetal idea I had was for a much more Realm-centric game, and I don't think it fits well within a world-hopping exploration game. How would you feel instead about an Orichalcum...pilgrim, of sorts? Like, a missionary who exists to convert the people of the worlds he finds to the service of the Great Maker (which is not at all the same thing as service to the Realm, and boy doesn't that piss off the Deliberative) and to dole out merciless justice according to the law of the Tome?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T15:46:53-08:00","id":56397,"title":"","content":"A vigilante Military Chaplain of sorts? That sounds like an awesome character idea, Jim. You can definitely do that.<br /> <br /> @Jotun: I can understand why you'd want them. Special guns are a staple of Science Fiction/Fantasy, and even with artifact/Alchemical weapons, firearm-type weapons would still be rare, precious items to come by. Hopefully, this way, you can have your big bag o' gunz if you're so inclined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","user":"Dietaku","date":".  We're moving too fast for the forum to catch up. 01-23-2014, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:00:32-08:00","id":56434,"title":"","content":"Hello Dietaku do you have an open spot left ? I would like to join","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:04:17-08:00","id":56437,"title":"","content":"@Magnusar: Definitely! I'd be glad to have you on. Do you have any ideas for your character concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:18:00-08:00","id":56450,"title":"","content":"Well I do have a dawn that I have prepared a while ago dual wielding a daiklave and a prayer piece clad in celestial battle armor a bit jaded basically a soldier and commander.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 01-23-2014, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:28:18-08:00","id":56456,"title":"","content":"That sounds good, Magnusar, although why he's jaded might be something to expand on. Cool, though. I think that can definitely work here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:34:54-08:00","id":56461,"title":"","content":"That's good to hear/read, I wanted to know what are the rules on character creation what you put was a bit unclear to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:44:48-08:00","id":56470,"title":"","content":"My rulings thus far have been:<br /> <br /> Standard Chargen for Gunstar, with flaws and merits allowed.<br /> <br /> You get 50 exp starting out.<br /> <br /> Prodigy grants charms at a discount, as per the merit suggestion. <br /> <br /> Firearms and Firearms artifacts are allowed, but are used with the Archery ability.<br /> <br /> I think that's it. Sorry I was unclear before. I have a tendency to ramble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","user":"Dietaku","date":". 01-23-2014, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:46:18-08:00","id":56471,"title":"","content":"@magnasaur yay, a tank to hide behind!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","user":"AlbztheDude","date":". 01-24-2014, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","name":"AlbztheDude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T18:01:02-08:00","id":56477,"title":"","content":"Cool I'll start right away also do you have restriction on charms that we can use like from the ink monkeys and such ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T18:03:29-08:00","id":56479,"title":"","content":"Just as a tip Magnusar, prayer pieces are at a slight disadvantage in this setting as Demons (well, Daeva) are not Creatures of Darkness. This means no Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Still, nifty idea. I'm tossing up the benefits of Armor of the Unseen Assassin myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T18:05:26-08:00","id":56480,"title":"","content":"There are no restrictions on charms, or even making your own. However, if you're using homebrew content, if you could tell me, so I could look it over beforehand, that would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T18:07:39-08:00","id":56482,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid I have to withdraw my name from consideration for this game. Best regards to everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T18:08:25-08:00","id":56483,"title":"","content":"Yeah I just read that shame... never mind I'll go with a shellcaster on this one as they are allowed more ammo but a bit less damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T18:12:16-08:00","id":56486,"title":"","content":"@Jim: Sorry to hear that. Best of regards to you too.<br /> <br /> @Magnusar: By all means, whatever weapons you like, that should be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","user":"Dietaku","date":". 01-23-2014, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T19:28:48-08:00","id":56532,"title":"","content":"It's never explained in the book or I haven't found it but is the great Curse in effect ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T20:56:01-08:00","id":56561,"title":"","content":"Several Primordials have been slain, including Sachervall, and Deathknights are somewhere out there. So, I'd say, yes, the Great Curse is in effect. Which means, if you want to take the Greater Curse flaw, then it is applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T10:40:32-08:00","id":56868,"title":"","content":"Do you accept custom power core there is one that I based on a hearthstone that one of my friend came up in a normal exalted game basically its power is that it counts as two level higher for the purpose of powering artifact is that too much ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T10:52:59-08:00","id":56876,"title":"","content":"Ok, working through a backstory. He was a well loved Lector with a gifted operatic voice. He is missing a hand from a voidspawn attack in his childhood and is terrified of them to this day. He Exalted when his performance was interrupted by two disagreeing exalts almost came to blows. He calmed them with a song of such beauty that they begged each other for forgiveness; earning him the name Harmonious Voice Virtuoso. As an Eclipse, he spends his time between diplomatic work for the Deliberative and doing his part as a voidfighter pilot for the Realm Defense Grid. Im considering between a few flaws to emphasize his childhood trauma. Should I stick to nightmares or will we encounter enough Voidspawn away from Auto to justify phobia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","name":"AlbztheDude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T11:58:38-08:00","id":56912,"title":"","content":"@Magnusar: That's fine. What name do you have for it, per chance?<br /> <br /> @Albz: I'd stick to nightmares. I don't think you'll see enough Voidspawn to merit the phobia. I like your back-story, though. A singing diplomat. That could definitely work, especially if he has a flashy enough outfit. <br /> <br /> I'm loving all of what y'all have shown me. I'm definitely getting pumped for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T12:09:06-08:00","id":56916,"title":"","content":"Hum... as for the name I don't have one maybe a Power Node or something I don't know yet. I took backing Gunstar Defense Line so that the character as a rank in the military is it you know useful in you're game setting considering that we are far from the gunstar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 01-24-2014, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T12:34:13-08:00","id":56931,"title":"","content":"I was just curious about the name. If you hadn't settled on one, that's fine.<br /> <br /> Considering that your ship and the crew are members of the Line Fleet? Yes, I think it would be, providing you with social benefits to the rest of the crew. Also, IIRC, it provides you with a Voidstar fighter for free if you take Backing 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T12:42:44-08:00","id":56937,"title":"","content":"Really !!! Cool done backing of at least 3 in the Gunstar Defense Line taken almost done with the character, I'll post it in the OoC thread when I am done, also can I spend XP to raise backgrounds ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T12:52:01-08:00","id":56949,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear you like the backstory and yea, I was thinking he be a fairly fancy dresser. Probably going roman senator with robes or a half cape draped over his stump. Another question. I was planning on grabbing some backing for the Realm Defense Grid, could I have a slightly customized Voidfighter. I was thinking mainly of changing the dragonblooded specific capabilities and making them solar themed instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","name":"AlbztheDude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T13:14:31-08:00","id":56969,"title":"","content":"@Magnusar: Yes, that's fine. Do so at a rate of 3 exp per dot, as per Scroll of Errata. Do note that I don't usually require Exp expenditure for backgrounds raised through roleplay, though.<br /> <br /> @Albz: Are you referring to the Dragon's Roar Engine? If so, that's fine, although what sort of energy would you be immune to? Solar/Infernal essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T15:57:34-08:00","id":57047,"title":"","content":"@dietaku yea the engine. I would figure solar essence I suppose. Im also not seeing exact rules for fighting in the ship. Namely how to defend. Like can I dodge attacks with it? What ability do I use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","name":"AlbztheDude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T16:38:04-08:00","id":57064,"title":"","content":"Pg. 31 in Wonders of the Lost Age. Dodging is part of Maneuverability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T16:45:17-08:00","id":57069,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that Jotun been wondering about that myself, also I have read the story you put its pretty nice, but I can't see you're character sheet though.<br /> <br /> Edit: Never mind it's there now sorry -_-'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 01-24-2014, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T19:08:26-08:00","id":57154,"title":"","content":"Hey Dietaku, are you still recruiting for this game?<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T19:15:15-08:00","id":57156,"title":"","content":"Don't quote me NutiketAiel but I think we've only filled 4 of the 6 slots, so you should be good. Also welcome aboard. provisionally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","name":"AlbztheDude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T19:28:25-08:00","id":57163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlbztheDude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=57156#post57156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't quote me NutiketAiel but I think we've only filled 4 of the 6 slots, so you should be good. Also welcome aboard. provisionally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've quoted you. :-P And thanks for the provisional welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T20:51:59-08:00","id":57204,"title":"","content":"I count 5 players (Myself, Jotun, Alectai, Albzthedude, Magnusar) confirmed by our glorious ST, but that still leaves a spot blank. And speaking as Dietaku's brother, I can say with 98, 99 percent certainty, that means recruitment is still open. So, (unless he says no just to prove me wrong), welcome aboard!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T21:59:44-08:00","id":57239,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Noodle.<br /> <br /> The concept I am currently considering is an Alchemical, specifically a Starmetal-caste Engineer-Priest, <i>Righteous Common Enterprise</i>. Since our team is being tasked with finding an appropriate location for a secret planetary base inside the Spiral, (s)he (I haven't settled on a gender yet) would be responsible for planning and preparing the infrastructure of the base, particularly in regard to the eventual mortal inhabitants. In the meantime, (s)he would be one of the main engineers on the ship (or maybe the chief engineer, if no other PC is planning to fill that role), a general mechanical/technical troubleshooter and artificer in addition to seeing to the needs of the mortal crew as a Champion. Assuming there are any mortal crew, that is; did you intend to have all the non-PCs be Terrestrial Exalts? In any case, I see this character as being more far-sighted. Less concerned about the prosecution of the war, (s)he is willing to trust in the Solar Deliberative to ensure that victory is achieved. (S)he is more concerned with making sure that victory is achieved righteously, and that a good and stable life for the mortals of the Realm will be waiting on the other side of this war.<br /> <br /> I have some more detailed ideas in mind, of course, but I wanted to run this general concept by you first, Dietaku, before I started getting into more detail. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T22:36:18-08:00","id":57259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=57204#post57204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I count 5 players (Myself, Jotun, Alectai, Albzthedude, Magnusar) confirmed by our glorious ST, but that still leaves a spot blank. And speaking as Dietaku's brother, I can say with 98, 99 percent certainty, that means recruitment is still open. So, (unless he says no just to prove me wrong), welcome aboard!</div> </div> </div> </div>NO. <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, joking aside, NukiteAiel, you're definitely welcome to join. I like your idea, too. Welcome aboard!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T04:31:38-08:00","id":57357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=57239#post57239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Righteous Common Enterprise</i></div> </div> </div> </div> I see what you did there. Also Welcome aboard more officially!<br /> <br /> Also @ Dietaku Will different languages be a thing? Or does everyone in the Spiral all speak Old Realm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","user":"AlbztheDude","date":". 01-25-2014, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1570-albzthedude","name":"AlbztheDude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T07:55:14-08:00","id":57436,"title":"","content":"Different languages will be a thing, but Old Realm will be the most common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T08:16:26-08:00","id":57446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=57259#post57259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NO.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, joking aside, NukiteAiel, you're definitely welcome to join. I like your idea, too. Welcome aboard!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you very much. Happy to be here. :-)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see what you did there. Also Welcome aboard more officially!<br /> <br /> Also @ Dietaku Will different languages be a thing? Or does everyone in the Spiral all speak Old Realm? </div> </div> </div>Thank you, also. Glad you liked what I did there. ;-) You know, the language thing always had me curious. In the First Age, why didn't they just call it &quot;Realm&quot;? Why was it &quot;Old Realm&quot;? Anyway, the decision is yours of course, Dietaku, but if you're looking for input, I would suggest that, after 4000 years of living in an environment totally alien to their home, some linguistic drift is in order. At the very least, I suggest two languages- Old Realm, still spoken by spirits and very old Exalts, as in the core setting, with the more commonly spoken Autochthonic (or whatever you want to call it) as a vernacular. Just my opinion, though. The Solar Deliberative certainly could very easily keep everyone speaking Old Realm if you want to keep it straightforward.<br /> <br /> Now I have to go to work shortly, so unfortunately I don't have time right this minute to get into my character sheet; I plan to have it up and posted tonight, after I get home. However, since you do approve my concept, I'll take a little time now to fill in some more details about what I'm thinking, and to ask a few questions. I still haven't settled on a gender yet, btw, but I get tired of writing (s)he and his/her, so I'm just going to use female pronouns for now. These are mostly just disjointed thoughts; I'll obviously write out a more coherent backstory to go with the character sheet tonight.<br /> <br /> <i>Righteous Common Enterprise</i> was exalted in Thutot, the capital of Gulak. Enterprise's purpose when she was created was to help Gulak deal with its overpopulation problems, both through architecture/urban planning and social engineering. As such, she is accomplished at both subjects and, while she did much good in Gulak, was ideal for the mission to help establish the first Realm facility in the Spiral; thus, she volunteered. She trusts the Solar Deliberative and their leadership, but worries that they lose touch of what she considers the true goal of the Realm, which is a better, safer life for all where everyone can flourish according to their merits. Exalted. Human. Spirits. Even Autochthon, once the Titans have been defeated and the need for the &quot;Gunstar&quot; has passed. With the (triumphant?) return to the Spiral to (successfully?) prosecute and conclude the war looming, Enterprise feels that it is the role of the Champions to begin preparing for what comes after the war. While the mission is to establish a military base in the Spiral, Enterprise's plans revolve more around creating the nucleus for a colony. It will fulfill its immediate primary function as a foothold for the invasion, of course, but it will also be the seed of infrastructure from which a true home can grow on this world. She plans to do everything in her power to ensure that humans are involved in the construction and operation of the facility from day one as an integral part, particularly humans from Gulak (which should also help with their overpopulation problem). Righteous Common Enterprise is quite religious, seeing herself as a devout (if free spirited) follower of Autochthon and his (remaining) divine ministers, as much a priestess as an engineer. She feels particularly close to Noi, and feels that many of the citizens of the Realm, human and exalted, focus so much on the war effort that the lose the simple joys that come from curiosity, innovation and even companionship; she works hard to ensure that the people she works with are both happy and connected with one another, and is a strong proponent of the polyamorous relationships that are common in Gulak. This is the first time her soul has been chosen to be an Alchemical Exalt; her past lives' heroism was mostly focused on bringing people together and helping to find innovative and new ways for them to cooperate, even when it went against the wishes of the established leadership. One of those past lives was as a Joybringer, and she feels a certain affinity towards the Maiden of Serenity as a result (though it is nothing like her devotion to Autochthon and Noi).<br /> <br /> How does all that sound?<br /> <br /> Now, a few questions. First, is our mission to simply find a site for the base, or to actually get it started while we're waiting for the fleet and Battlestar Autochthonia to arrive? Will there be a substantial number of humans among our crew? Or any humans, for that matter? Both for the mission and as initial personnel for the base?<br /> <br /> I was considering a familiar, a minor construct or maybe machine spirit, possibly sent to Righteous Common Enterprise by Noi to help and guide her. Maybe something mongoose or ferret like in appearance and function, though I haven't decided for certain yet. Or maybe something monkey-like. Whatever the form, would that be acceptable?<br /> <br /> A Warstrider or Voidfighter would definitely not be appropriate for Righteous Common Enterprise, but I am thinking about something that would allow her freedom of movement in the void, particularly during space battles, so she can make repairs to the ship or to voidfighters etc from the outside if necessary. Maybe some kind of power armor or suit, or maybe a small pod or shuttle or other type of repair ship or something, or maybe just a combination of a few minor artifacts and alchemical charms to enable her to get around. Would you be willing to work with me on this? Do you have any ideas of what would work best?<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's what I have so far. I'll check back in tonight after work.<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":". 01-25-2014, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T20:37:32-08:00","id":57865,"title":"","content":"You raise a number of excellent points, Nukite--Jim. Can I call you Jim? I like your user name, but I feel like I'm always misspelling it. Anyways, machine spirit familiar? Like a weasel or monkey? No problem. I assume, of course, you're going the &quot;Smart, but physically weak&quot; route for your familiar? <br /> <br /> I also thought that Alchemicals didn't need to breathe; the main danger of being exposed to the void? Be that as it may, I would imagine that most powered armors would grant you immunity to the Void and its air-based environmental dangers. Alternatively, you could get Phoenix Wing Pinions. Those would allow you to traverse the Void. Either that, or a custom charm. Whichever.<br /> <br /> As for the mission, I thought you would be the ones setting it up. As I said before, I imagined a military force of about a thousand DBs, along with the PCs. However, I hadn't considered the numbers for logistics of building a base. Therefore, I'll say, &quot;About ten thousand&quot; mortals, due to needs of maintaining factory cathedrals, and consturction efforts once you get there. Also, the fact that Zekka, the Alchemical Patropolis, despises being overcrowded, and therefore, the Realm military couldn't place the estimated fifteen thousand workers on this mission.<br /> <br /> As for Languages? Well....You guys forced my hand a little. <br /> <br /> Cultural differences between the Spiral and the Gunstar ought to produce significant differences in syntax, as you say, Jim. Therefore, as your point, I will give you this map. You'll need it to understand the next bits.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s27.postimg.org/gw4ekxwib/Spiral.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> As per regular Exalted, I divided the Spiral into five regions. The &quot;arms&quot; are both large twisting nexuses of Essence, holding the Elemental Poles in place, along with large clumps of planets. In the center if the &quot;Elemental Pole of Earth&quot; holding aloft the Viridian Plaza, the seat of Theion's government, the Congress of Daevas, and the center of the Titanic Exalted's operations. There, Ligier, and Rathia, the Crystal Moon (Other Fetich of Theion) both perch in the Sky-Vault over the Spiral. The point being, each arm has its own dialect of Realm, analogous to the directional dialects, so as to allow the Titans to focus more time on themselves, and to a lesser extent, the war against the Exalted. Realm, though, is the language of choice for Daevas and Infernals, thanks in part to Theion being a stickler for it, and Ta'akozoka's Guild using it as their trade language.<br /> <br /> As for the planet names? Well, you guy's'll have to go there to find out what they're all about.<br /> <br /> I've read your all's characters. They look good. Now, I have some questions for you:<br /> <br /> A Lunar Captain of the Marines, a la Mr. Worf. Would you want one, a sort of liasion to the Terrestrial troops? Also, how much flavor do oyu want for your DBs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T21:11:10-08:00","id":57890,"title":"","content":"LOL, yes, you can call me Jim. That's why I sign my posts that way, so that you guys can call me that rather than having to type &quot;Nutiket&quot; or &quot;NutiketAiel&quot; all the time. ;-)<br /> <br /> You are correct that Alchemicals do not need to breathe. However, the other effects of hard vacuum are still a problem for them. See the sidebar, &quot;Surviving in Space,&quot; on page 23 of Shards of the Exalted Dream. There is an Alchemical charm that will do the job, but Enterprise will not meet the prerequisites (no way she's going to have a Stamina of 4). I'm thinking of just going with a 2-dot artifact as the sidebar suggests to survive the void, but I'd rather it not be a full spacesuit, as I don't like the image of an alchemical in a spacesuit. Would you be OK with something more visually low-key, like a force field belt or something?<br /> <br /> Thank you for the clarification on languages. Has their been sufficient contact (through espionage, prisoners, or whatever) between the crew of Autochthon and the inhabitants of the Spiral for the characters to start with knowledge of their direction tongues, or is that not feasible given the isolation? I ask not for Righteous Common Enterprise, as it wouldn't be something she would learn in any case, but just for general info, or if one of the other PCs is interested. Though, I suppose it wouldn't hurt to have an Air Aspect linguist to run our communications gear for us; I suggest Sato Hoshi. ;-)<br /> <br /> I suppose I wouldn't object to a Lunar Marine captain, though I worry a little about another celestial stealing some thunder from the PCs. You'd just have to handle it carefully, I suppose. What do you mean by &quot;flavor&quot; for the Terrestrials? I mean, obviously we're not expecting you to write up full characters for 1000 troops (well, I'm not, anyway), but I figure there will be some with whom we regularly interact. Like Hoshi the comm officer. And some of the pilots, since we have two pilot PCs to hang in the ready room with them.<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T18:18:05-08:00","id":58441,"title":"","content":"Ah, cool. Thanks<br /> <br /> I apologize for the misconception about the durability of Alchemicals, though. Your belt idea sounds fine.Actually, the force field belts from Dune come to mind. Maybe you can get a soak benefit from it, too?<br /> <br /> Fair enough about the Lunar marine. I suppose I'll keep them as the captain of the<i> Mercury's Delight,</i> then. As for the DBs, oh, hohohohoho. LORD NO, about fleshing out a thousand Terrestrials. I have a Sworn Brotherhood or two in mind, largely culled from other games I've STed for, which I think may be of use to you. Just wondering if you'd all would mind having them along or if you want to have faceless DB grunts, is all. Speaking of it, though, I like your idea for Comm Ops Hoshi. I'm going to use him now.<br /> <br /> Finally, as per languages, I imagine that there has been enough of an exchange that Solar and Lunar linguists figured out the nuances of the Directional Tongues. Maybe not every word, and not perfectly accentless, but easily enough to be understood clearly. Also, because I forgot to mention it, Yu Shan is still a thing. It is directly above the Viridian Plaza. What's there, and who's doing what to it, well...You'll have to see<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T19:52:46-08:00","id":58480,"title":"","content":"That's good to know my character only speak old realm (no linguistic) and yeah I like the idea of some personalized Dragon-Blooded since I hope to form my own elite Dragon-Blooded Space Marine/pilots unit. there is something I'd like to know a bit more about the details of who or what else is on the scouting mission with us ? there are dragon-blooded but are other celestial exalted and Alchemicals except for the ship and PCs ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 01-27-2014, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T08:46:41-08:00","id":58745,"title":"","content":"Well, that's a bit of a question, but here goes.<br /> <br /> Zekka is outfitted with a Vat Complex, two Factory Cathedrals, and the staff necesary to maintain them all. If he desired, he could produce new Alchemicals, should he possess the required materials, as the required technicians are among his crew as service and maintenance staff, such is the import of this mission.<br /> <br /> Zekka himself? Well, there's a reason he's called the <i>Radical Mendicant</i>. When he was younger, he strode among the stars, a boon companion of the famous Sun Dragon, that Dawn Caste who cast down the Fog of Ten Thousand Fangs into the lower reaches of the Spiral. He battled Human and Daeva alike, a firebrand who saw the stratified society of both the Spiral and to a lesser extent, the Gunstar stifling. The Gunstar chiefs of staff couldn't do anything about the Starmetal Alchemical; he fought too hard to bench, and they were afraid to do so anyways; he may very well destroy valuable resources out of boredom. Thus, when he ascended to Patropoli-hood, his city was made into a star-faring battleship not only to sate his wanderlust, but also to keep him away from the Gusntar for as long as possible. In his human form, he stands a good 6 feet tall, usually dressed in leather, his distinctive dreaded cable hair a unique sight whenever he deigns to walk around.<br /> <br /> Zekka is also armed to the teeth, with five implosion bow batteries, four essence cannons, and seven lightning casters. He also possesses the unique weapon set of two gigantic arms sprouting beneath his superstructure. Ever a martial artist, Zekka demanded their addition, so &quot;He can once again smash his enemies with his own fists.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Mercury's Delight</i> is a Mela-class fast cruiser, a ship designed for fast and long cruises, and possesses only a fraction of Zekka's firepower and resilience. She can bring to bear three essence cannons, an implosion bow, and one anti-air essence net.<br /> <br /> Her captain, Kana Kleiner, is a Full Moon Lunar, She is a Void Serpent (Those forty foot feathered snakes who glide through the Void with ease) Totem naval commander, born and bred. However, she's also an eccentric; preferring to wander her ship as tiny forms of whatever form she feels at the time. She also keeps a small zoo along with her for her own amusement. These quirks haven't earned her any favors, but her talents at naval fighting cannot be denied.<br /> <br /> There are several Sworn Brotherhoods under the Directional Animal Genses, those famous martial families organized by the Sidereal Elder, Peerless Ocelot, for the express purpose of creating strong martial traditions to further the war effort. Also, amongst the Terrestrial host is Sato Hoshi, a mild-mannered man who is related to the great Savant, Ledaal. While his talents are nowhere near his ancestor's, his gift for langauge is great, and a valued asset on this mission.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, that answers your question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","user":"Dietaku","date":". 01-27-2014, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T10:08:42-08:00","id":58828,"title":"","content":"Yep, that's exactly what I wanted to know, I think me and Zekka are gonna get along just fine. We do have quite a bit of resources that we can access it is good to know, also I have finish my character just need to post my combat stats and personality trait and its gonna be done so if something is not okay with it just tell me and I'll make the change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T10:33:25-08:00","id":58858,"title":"","content":"Glad you like it, and if anything comes up when I read your character, I'll let you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:03:24-08:00","id":59111,"title":"","content":"Liking the writeups! One question: how are you fitting us into all of this? Are we a team that goes out on <i>Mercury's Delight</i> and survey's new planets, or are we there when Zekka lands and the troops get shifted out (or a bit of both)? Are we meant to stay together as a team the entire time, or be able to split up a bit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:18:11-08:00","id":59128,"title":"","content":"You all are the officer corps of Zekka. <i>Mercury's Delight</i> is your escort and backup. Zekka will be your base of operations, and from him, you'll go down and survey potential planets. You're free to split up if you so wish, and some can even stay aboard <i>Mercury's Delight</i> if you want. Zekka is atmospherically capable, but he'll also have landing craft if you'd prefer to go down in a more low-key way. <br /> <br /> If I can illustrate this is a better way, Your expedition is akin to the Enterprise and Voyager. One is bigger and badder and can do more things, but the other is faster, but weaker. You're the Officers of the Etnerprise. Or so. I'm not entirely up on my Star Trek as much as I once was....<br /> <br /> I hope that helps. I'm aiming for a Wednesday start time, as everyone seems more or less done. If you do need more time, ; that's fine, and we can work you in, but I'd like to, probably the same as y'all, get this thing going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T18:26:59-08:00","id":59360,"title":"","content":"ST-man: Posted the mechanical side of my Siddie in the OOC thread by editing my place-holder post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T11:08:16-08:00","id":59966,"title":"","content":"is it still too late to come up with something? I've been brainstorming over the weekend while I had reduced internet access.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2067-alectai","name":"Alectai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T11:55:26-08:00","id":60010,"title":"","content":"That's fine, Alectai. That's why I asked before I started. If you need more time, that's cool. What were you thinking for your concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T18:07:57-08:00","id":60270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=58441#post58441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, cool. Thanks<br /> <br /> I apologize for the misconception about the durability of Alchemicals, though. Your belt idea sounds fine.Actually, the force field belts from Dune come to mind. Maybe you can get a soak benefit from it, too?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I can live with that; how much of a soak benefit? Your call.<br /> <br /> Also, may I have your permission to combine the two dot Precision Goggles and the one dot Essence-Scrying Visor into a single 3 dot artifact? Do you consider that combination to be an appropriate power level for a 3 dot artifact, or should I tone it up or down?<br /> <br /> As for Sato Hoshi, I'm glad you like the idea, but since you mentioned you're not entirely up on your Star Trek Fu, I thought I might point out that the name was kind of a joke on my part. No need to change what you have in mind, though. <a href=\"http://en.memory-alpha.org/wiki/Hoshi_Sato\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.memory-alpha.org/wiki/Hoshi_Sato</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T18:19:37-08:00","id":60279,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm. How about +3 to all soaks, and stackable with armor?<br /> <br /> Also, as per the super goggles, that's fine. It reminded me of<br /> <img src=\"http://i880.photobucket.com/albums/ac10/Dietaku/tumblr_mup48owhaN1rb06tgo1_r1_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> And that made me chuckle.<br /> <br /> As for Ms. Hoshi. Oops. My interpretation of her was that she was in fact, a he. Such is the lack of easily discernible gender signifiers in Japanese names, I guess. Oh, well. I guess people won't mistake Ledaal Sato Hoshi and the Enterprise crew member, then.<br /> <br /> Also, in case you missed it, the IC thread is up and running, albeit in a &quot;Pre-operation&quot; mindset right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T18:24:53-08:00","id":60283,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I saw that the IC thread was up, but I wanted to complete my character sheet first; I am working on it right now and should have it done within the next... hour-ish, I hope.<br /> <br /> As for the belt, that sounds a little overpowered to me. It's only a 2 dot artifact, and even though it doesn't need to supply air like the normal version, +3 seems like a little much, perhaps +2?<br /> <br /> Thank you for the approval for the visor. What is that picture from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T18:30:44-08:00","id":60288,"title":"","content":"(Mutters something about needing to keep Wonders on him whenever he posts lest he place his God-stomping Boots in his Glorious Piehole more than he does)<br /> <br /> That sounds fair, and I appreciate you bringing that up. Very sporting. <br /> <br /> No problem about the goggles. The gif is from Kill La Kill, a goofy fighting anime airing at present. The picture is Omiko Hakodate, a tennis enthusiast whose attack style wouldn't be far from how I envision high-level Solar thrown charms being like. I'd recommend it so long as goofy, fan service outfits don't bother you. Both heroines have battle outfits which amount to thong swimsuits, y'see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T18:34:07-08:00","id":60290,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see.<br /> <br /> So, since the Gunstar Defense Line is more or less a military organization... how do you plan to handle rank among the PCs? Should we all have a rank?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T18:45:09-08:00","id":60298,"title":"","content":"I think that ranks would definitely add flavor to your character. If I'm remembering right, you all took more or less equal dots in Backing, so you'd all be about the same level in your respective Division, as you all seemed to take to different substrata of the Gunstar military. Pellias being Deliberative Army, Amelia being a Gunstar Flygirl, Jin being a SAS Spook, and the like. I don't really have a rank system in mind, so if you want to give yourself an ostentatious title, that should be fine. So, rest assured, there won't be any one commander of the Expedition; that's not really fun when that happens, and you all are contributing in your own ways, anyways.<br /> <br /> And if need be, Zekka can decide for himself what happens to him, although I don't think that will come up much. Hopefully, that answers your question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T18:50:56-08:00","id":60301,"title":"","content":"Well that is good to know although I based my character more on a combat officer, so I will most likely order the dragon-blooded and the mortals around but never the PCs we are all celestial Exalted and thus equal, thought I think I might have the highest backing in the Gunstar Defense Line so I took the liberty of giving myself the title of commander.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 01-28-2014, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T18:56:45-08:00","id":60306,"title":"","content":"As a Dawn Caste, you probably would have overall command of the Expedition, Magnusar, but having checked, it does seem you do. If you want to be &quot;Supreme Wing Commander: Electric Space Fighter&quot; as opposed to just &quot;Commander,&quot; that's fine.<br /> <br /> I'm glad we're all coming together on this, though. I like it! I'll post more in the IC thread in a bit. Life calls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T20:43:14-08:00","id":60386,"title":"","content":"OK, character history done, pending ST approval (of course). Also provided a more detailed explanation for the various backgrounds, especially Allies and Followers. These are all supposed to be NPCs, obviously, so I built them with the intention of giving our dear ST something to work with. If you'd like me to change anything about any of them, Dietaku, please let me know. All that's left is the character appearance, which unfortunately I just don't have time for right this minute. I'll get to it as soon as I can (hopefully tomorrow).<br /> <br /> So, are you OK with my sheet, Dietaku? Anything you need me to change, or explain?<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T20:59:40-08:00","id":60401,"title":"","content":"No, Jim, Enterprise looks good. I also like how you interwove your character's back-story with that of Zekka's. Great work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","user":"Dietaku","date":".  SPELLING ERROR! 01-28-2014, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T23:47:59-08:00","id":60519,"title":"","content":"Excellent, thank you Dietaku. I try my best, with back story, backgrounds and merits/flaws, to give the ST tools to tell their story. You are fine with Enterprise's family? You are fine with the characters expressed through Allies and Followers? I am not averse to changing any of it if you want to, if something else would work better with what you have in mind, or if there is an NPC you already have that you would like me to use rather than the ones I have sketched out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T01:47:35-08:00","id":60566,"title":"","content":"So, just for clarity, is Amelia the captain of the ship, or just the commander of the air group (the pilots and void fighter crews and such)? It is your call, Dietaku, but I must caution you, in almost every game I've been in or seen where one PC is given military-style authority over most or all of the other PCs, it's ended badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T04:58:42-08:00","id":60639,"title":"","content":"Don't worry about that I have no intention of trying to order any PCs around that's what the NPCs a there for, beside I had the same type of experience as the one you speak of, so don't worry about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 01-29-2014, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T07:05:41-08:00","id":60732,"title":"","content":"No, I was just commenting about ranks, I don't expect, and would seriously frown on, Magnusar getting an imperious attitude. So, rest assured, you and I, and it seems, Magnusar, are all of one mind on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T07:14:30-08:00","id":60738,"title":"","content":"Well and good, and I hope it works out. Still, from an IC perspective, I need to know whether I should be referring to Amelia as Commander of the Air Group, or as Commander of the expedition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T07:57:22-08:00","id":60770,"title":"","content":"She's commander of the Air Group. I don't think Magnusar settled on an official rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T14:39:39-08:00","id":61073,"title":"","content":"No not really i picked commander because it was more of generic rank than anything else and for the fluff never forget the fluff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T20:06:40-08:00","id":61260,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the clarification Dietaku.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T20:53:30-08:00","id":61285,"title":"","content":"You're welcome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T07:57:50-08:00","id":83954,"title":"","content":"If anyone is interested, I'm reopening recruitment for my game. If interested, please post here. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T14:05:11-07:00","id":139765,"title":"","content":"Quick character concept to see if it fits in with the rest. Lunar exalted (I don't know caste yet) with a preference for stealth and thrown weapons. He is relatively young and hasn't yet had the opportunity to amass the various battle forms that other Lunars use. Motivation: to punish the Tyrant Sun for the injuries he inflicted on Luna.<br /> <br /> I'll get the character built and posted to the OoC thread as soon as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3025-kelsyk","name":"kelsyk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T14:28:39-07:00","id":139801,"title":"","content":"Yeah fresh meat for the grinder lol, nice to have you with us Kelsyk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T22:00:30-07:00","id":140250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kelsyk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/54991-recruitment-exaltled-2-5-gunstar-autochthonia-to-boldly-go?p=139765#post139765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick character concept to see if it fits in with the rest. Lunar exalted (I don't know caste yet) with a preference for stealth and thrown weapons. He is relatively young and hasn't yet had the opportunity to amass the various battle forms that other Lunars use. Motivation: to punish the Tyrant Sun for the injuries he inflicted on Luna.<br /> <br /> I'll get the character built and posted to the OoC thread as soon as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good, Kelysk, and glad to have you aboard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T12:39:28-07:00","id":143797,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall missing this before. If there is still room, I would be most interested! If there is, I will give a quick look over to who is here already and what is going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T15:46:00-07:00","id":143924,"title":"","content":"Alrighty, Exthalion. Glad to have you! <br /> <br /> To answer Kelsyk's question from before, the game has largely been about planetary exploration, and less ship-side fighting, although if that's something that is desired, I'll be down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}